WEBVTT

00:00:09.376 --> 00:00:12.641
I'm not so fundamentally enthusiastic

00:00:13.413 --> 00:00:16.382
Even I will participate in this

00:00:17.017 --> 00:00:20.153
It's been a long time since we went for a drive

00:00:20.153 --> 00:00:22.417
Everyone is excited

00:00:22.989 --> 00:00:25.287
He's coming too

00:00:25.625 --> 00:00:28.822
I may have no chance with him right now

00:00:29.696 --> 00:00:32.563
But I'm definitely going

00:00:33.199 --> 00:00:38.603
If you've got a good poker face

00:00:39.372 --> 00:00:41.741
There will be something

00:00:41.741 --> 00:00:45.812
Let's head to the mountains

00:00:45.812 --> 00:00:48.781
We'll just get sunburned at the sea

00:00:49.916 --> 00:00:53.920
Even though it's coat season

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:58.357
He is completely misunderstanding

00:00:58.625 --> 00:01:02.595
What's going on?

00:01:02.595 --> 00:01:06.566
Being this happy

00:01:06.566 --> 00:01:14.439
I'm laughing so hard I might burst

00:01:14.808 --> 00:01:22.982
I get choked up when I see his back

00:01:22.982 --> 00:01:30.889
In the whirlpool of an endless smile

00:01:33.927 --> 00:01:36.259
Mom, watch! I can dive!

00:01:36.596 --> 00:01:37.697
Mom, watch!

00:01:37.697 --> 00:01:39.130
I'm watching!

00:01:48.441 --> 00:01:50.705
Herve! Herve!

00:01:51.244 --> 00:01:54.013
Look at Mom! Hurry! Hurry, Herve!

00:01:54.013 --> 00:01:54.547
Mom!

00:01:54.547 --> 00:01:55.014
Mom?
Mom!

00:01:55.014 --> 00:01:55.815
Mom?
Mom! Mom! Mom! Hey, Mom!

00:01:55.815 --> 00:01:58.079
Mom! Mom! Mom! Hey, Mom!

00:01:58.885 --> 00:02:00.120
Mom! Mom! Mom! Mom! Mom! Mom!
Hey, open up!

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:00.820
Mom! Mom! Mom! Mom! Mom! Mom!

00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:01.688
Mom! Mom! Mom! Mom! Mom! Mom!
Herve! No! Stop it!

00:02:01.688 --> 00:02:02.455
Hurry! What? There are doctors on standby?!
Mom! Mom! Mom! Mom! Mom! Mom!
Herve! No! Stop it!

00:02:02.455 --> 00:02:04.624
Hurry! What? There are doctors on standby?!
Mom! Mom! Mom! Mom! Mom! Mom!

00:02:04.624 --> 00:02:08.094
No! Let go of me, Uncle! Mom! Mom!

00:02:08.094 --> 00:02:08.795
Herve!

00:02:08.795 --> 00:02:09.529
Mom! Mom!
Herve!

00:02:09.529 --> 00:02:11.664
Mom! Mom!

00:02:11.664 --> 00:02:16.294
Mom! Mom! Mom...

00:02:36.789 --> 00:02:38.256
Her heart has stopped.

00:02:38.892 --> 00:02:40.382
Will it start?

00:02:51.371 --> 00:02:53.839
There it is! You've got the belt on her,
right?! Hold her down!

00:02:54.007 --> 00:02:55.304
Damn!

00:02:58.144 --> 00:03:01.147
Mom! Mom! Mom!

00:03:01.147 --> 00:03:02.916
You got to keep her held down no
matter what! Hold her down!

00:03:02.916 --> 00:03:03.249
Mom! Mom! Mom!

00:03:03.249 --> 00:03:06.275
Herve, what are you doing?!
Get out of here! Get outside!
Mom! Mom! Mom!

00:03:06.753 --> 00:03:10.780
Mom! Mom! Mom!

00:03:15.128 --> 00:03:16.390
Mom?

00:03:18.264 --> 00:03:20.528
Mom? Mom?

00:03:25.672 --> 00:03:31.235
Mom! Mom! Mom! Mom!

00:03:32.946 --> 00:03:37.076
Episode #7
Another Fate

00:03:49.128 --> 00:03:50.597
We still haven't heard yesterday's
results, have we?

00:03:50.597 --> 00:03:51.598
Oh, no.
We still haven't heard yesterday's
results, have we?

00:03:51.598 --> 00:03:52.899
Well, I heard someone say it didn't
go too badly at any rate.

00:03:52.899 --> 00:03:54.298
Hey, Herve...

00:03:55.134 --> 00:03:57.728
Mireille's fever is down,

00:03:58.004 --> 00:03:59.806
but there's something wrong with her,
isn't there?

00:03:59.806 --> 00:04:04.903
Her throat is always dry, and she's
been taking a ton of medication.

00:04:05.345 --> 00:04:07.074
Uh, yeah...

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:09.271
She fell asleep again too.

00:04:09.983 --> 00:04:14.020
This new medicine works well.
She'll be fine before you know it.

00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:15.146
Really?

00:04:15.288 --> 00:04:17.756
Even Dr. Bender said so, remember?

00:04:18.024 --> 00:04:19.025
But...

00:04:19.025 --> 00:04:20.515
You're always worrying, Anna.

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:23.924
To me it seems like she's doing
better than last week.

00:04:24.697 --> 00:04:25.857
You think so?

00:04:26.165 --> 00:04:30.158
Yeah, everything will be fine.
Mireille will definitely get better.

00:04:30.803 --> 00:04:31.792
Yeah...

00:04:35.375 --> 00:04:36.376
I'll go get the test reagent.

00:04:36.376 --> 00:04:39.243
I'll start in two hours.
I guess we'll have to wait till then.

00:04:54.260 --> 00:04:55.261
Mireille?

00:04:55.261 --> 00:04:57.695
Doctor, I want to know the truth.

00:04:57.830 --> 00:04:58.931
The truth about?

00:04:58.931 --> 00:05:00.626
What is Mireille's condition?

00:05:02.268 --> 00:05:04.668
We need to observe her condition a little longer.

00:05:05.004 --> 00:05:08.374
There's no need to worry. We need to
give this new medicine a try.

00:05:08.374 --> 00:05:10.899
I want to hear about
the manifestation of the condition.

00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:12.345
Manifestation of the condition?

00:05:12.345 --> 00:05:14.643
Is her condition going to manifest soon?

00:05:16.449 --> 00:05:18.542
Who did you hear about this from?

00:05:19.519 --> 00:05:22.622
It's just that her recovery is taking
longer due to the fact that

00:05:22.622 --> 00:05:24.419
her immune system is weakened.

00:05:24.724 --> 00:05:26.392
And so what are you going to do?

00:05:26.392 --> 00:05:29.190
She's your cousin, right? You have
to help her keep her spirits up.

00:05:29.896 --> 00:05:31.056
Okay...

00:05:32.965 --> 00:05:34.990
Right, uh-huh...

00:05:35.702 --> 00:05:36.903
Yes, and then?

00:05:36.903 --> 00:05:39.269
Well, as we stand,
I have explained the medication,

00:05:39.605 --> 00:05:41.402
but I don't think he's convinced.

00:05:43.076 --> 00:05:45.778
How long does it look like Mireille
will be able to hold on?

00:05:45.778 --> 00:05:47.413
She's been doing well for a few days,

00:05:47.413 --> 00:05:50.314
but she could come down with
a fever at any time.

00:05:51.217 --> 00:05:52.582
It's just hard to say at this time.

00:05:53.119 --> 00:05:54.143
And Herve?

00:05:54.687 --> 00:05:58.487
A guard has confirmed that
he has left the building.

00:05:58.925 --> 00:06:00.256
I see...

00:06:16.008 --> 00:06:24.784
Haruka na koe watashi ni todoke
A distant voice reaches me

00:06:24.784 --> 00:06:27.186
Hey, look! Over here! Over here! Look!
Haruka na koe watashi ni todoke
A distant voice reaches me

00:06:27.186 --> 00:06:28.380
Hey, look! Over here! Over here! Look!

00:06:29.722 --> 00:06:32.625
You be careful, now. Don't go running like that.
Me wo samasuto
And when I open my eyes

00:06:32.625 --> 00:06:34.927
Me wo samasuto
And when I open my eyes

00:06:34.927 --> 00:06:35.762
Here I go! Watch!

00:06:35.762 --> 00:06:37.864
Here I go! Watch!
Katari tsukusu
It tells me all

00:06:37.864 --> 00:06:41.163
Katari tsukusu
It tells me all

00:06:43.503 --> 00:06:54.675
Anata no koe futari ni todoke
The two of them hear your voice

00:06:57.183 --> 00:07:08.959
Tanoshimi sae amae no you
And it seems even their joy depends on it

00:07:10.029 --> 00:07:22.669
Watashi no koe de wa mou ikenakute
I can't do it with my voice any longer

00:07:23.743 --> 00:07:39.580
Wazuka nagara demo sabishisa wo keshite
It may be trifling, but take my Ioneliness away...

00:07:42.061 --> 00:07:44.664
One place where research is being conducted

00:07:44.664 --> 00:07:49.260
on such linguistic characteristics is Paraguay.

00:07:49.602 --> 00:07:53.299
The two languages in question
being Spanish and Guarani.

00:07:53.506 --> 00:07:57.276
About eighty percent of the total population
speaks Guarani as their mother tongue,

00:07:57.276 --> 00:08:01.610
while only about six percent speak
Spanish as their mother tongue.

00:08:01.781 --> 00:08:03.339
Therefore, those who...
What do you mean by that?

00:08:03.683 --> 00:08:07.553
I guess it's like I've lost my will to act.

00:08:07.553 --> 00:08:08.520
Yeah?

00:08:09.355 --> 00:08:11.346
I just don't feel like doing anything.

00:08:11.524 --> 00:08:13.492
Isn't that how you always feel?

00:08:13.593 --> 00:08:14.924
No, that's not it!

00:08:16.162 --> 00:08:20.066
What I'm saying is, it's like I've
fallen into a deep hole.

00:08:20.066 --> 00:08:20.700
Yeah?

00:08:20.700 --> 00:08:21.234
And it's like I'm thinking,
"I'm going to die here."
Yeah?

00:08:21.234 --> 00:08:24.570
And it's like I'm thinking,
"I'm going to die here."

00:08:24.570 --> 00:08:26.697
But then, at the bottom, I find
what might be a way out.

00:08:26.973 --> 00:08:29.464
Uh, what?

00:08:30.009 --> 00:08:33.240
Well, it's like I thought I'd
be so happy about it,

00:08:33.779 --> 00:08:35.872
but in reality I'm not.

00:08:36.582 --> 00:08:40.313
It's just, I feel like my will to act
has disappeared.

00:08:40.653 --> 00:08:44.384
Huh? A way out at the bottom of a hole...

00:08:44.690 --> 00:08:46.385
Hey, it's just an analogy!

00:08:49.829 --> 00:08:52.064
Yuan, you really are useless, aren't you?!

00:08:52.064 --> 00:08:55.966
Hey, that's not true.
I mean, besides you called me, right?

00:08:56.536 --> 00:08:58.437
God, she's mean!

00:08:58.437 --> 00:09:00.564
Claire, wait up!

00:09:04.243 --> 00:09:06.108
Take them back.

00:09:06.679 --> 00:09:10.342
By your own hands, take back your real lives.

00:09:12.485 --> 00:09:14.282
So, that will do it for today.

00:09:14.787 --> 00:09:18.689
All of your reports are due for the next class.

00:09:22.962 --> 00:09:24.054
Can I have a minute?

00:09:26.799 --> 00:09:28.734
Kate, don't you think that

00:09:28.734 --> 00:09:31.601
recently you've been forgetting that
you're a member of Grace?

00:09:32.004 --> 00:09:32.438
What?

00:09:32.438 --> 00:09:33.005
You've been late a lot.
What?

00:09:33.005 --> 00:09:33.906
You've been late a lot.

00:09:33.906 --> 00:09:35.441
And you've left early too.

00:09:35.441 --> 00:09:38.171
But what I really want to say is this:

00:09:39.211 --> 00:09:41.771
You're not fulfilling any of your duties
as a member of Grace, are you?

00:09:41.981 --> 00:09:42.982
I...

00:09:42.982 --> 00:09:44.847
What about student checks?

00:09:45.151 --> 00:09:48.450
The data you gave us hasn't
been updated, you know?

00:09:48.921 --> 00:09:53.059
Is it your plan to make us do all the work that
makes us disliked by the other students?

00:09:53.059 --> 00:09:54.060
That's not...

00:09:54.060 --> 00:09:57.291
Observing the other students isn't a fun job,

00:09:57.763 --> 00:09:59.754
and none of us wants to be disliked.

00:09:59.899 --> 00:10:03.402
Jessica can't even make friends if she wants to.

00:10:03.402 --> 00:10:05.097
That's... fine.

00:10:05.438 --> 00:10:09.238
Because I realize that's just a part
of being a member of Grace.

00:10:10.142 --> 00:10:14.374
You don't do anything,
and yet, Paula's watching out for you.

00:10:14.614 --> 00:10:16.048
Why is that?

00:10:16.048 --> 00:10:17.049
I...

00:10:17.049 --> 00:10:19.745
You don't know?!
That's what I thought you'd say.

00:10:20.219 --> 00:10:22.084
You're more vicious than you look, aren't you?

00:10:22.288 --> 00:10:22.888
What?

00:10:22.888 --> 00:10:23.456
It's pretty easy to add up, isn't it?
What?

00:10:23.456 --> 00:10:24.616
It's pretty easy to add up, isn't it?

00:10:24.857 --> 00:10:26.449
That's not...

00:10:26.659 --> 00:10:28.593
I absolutely will not accept it!

00:10:36.836 --> 00:10:40.033
Rose, you're always out of it.

00:10:40.473 --> 00:10:42.304
And today, in particular,
you're out of it, aren't you?

00:10:42.775 --> 00:10:43.776
Huh?

00:10:43.776 --> 00:10:45.678
It seems like your mind is somewhere else.

00:10:45.678 --> 00:10:48.977
No, that's not true! I'm listening to you!

00:10:50.316 --> 00:10:52.045
I wasn't talking about anything!

00:10:54.186 --> 00:10:55.881
Don't try to just laugh it away!

00:10:58.057 --> 00:10:59.422
Has something happened?

00:11:00.059 --> 00:11:01.651
No, nothing.

00:11:02.528 --> 00:11:04.018
Really!

00:11:04.430 --> 00:11:05.988
You're being secretive again.

00:11:08.267 --> 00:11:10.970
Recently, Rose, you've been very secretive.

00:11:10.970 --> 00:11:13.139
I'm not keeping secrets or anything.

00:11:13.139 --> 00:11:14.240
Whatever, I don't care.

00:11:14.240 --> 00:11:15.708
Oh, by the way, Sara...

00:11:15.708 --> 00:11:16.868
What?

00:11:17.677 --> 00:11:18.871
I, uh...

00:11:20.513 --> 00:11:25.143
If tomorrow everything you had was gone...

00:11:25.551 --> 00:11:27.186
Is that what you were lost in thought over?

00:11:27.186 --> 00:11:29.780
No, it's nothing. Nothing!

00:11:34.627 --> 00:11:39.860
Do you think that from here on,
it'll be nothing but fun times?

00:11:40.132 --> 00:11:42.066
What? Why do you ask that all of a sudden?

00:11:42.501 --> 00:11:46.528
I was just wondering what you thought about it.

00:11:47.840 --> 00:11:50.502
I don't think about things like
"from here on" very much.

00:11:51.110 --> 00:11:53.476
Oh, I see.

00:11:54.714 --> 00:11:58.206
Yeah, you're right.

00:11:59.118 --> 00:12:00.312
What's up?

00:12:03.089 --> 00:12:05.591
If I can have fun now and
tonight, I'm content.

00:12:05.591 --> 00:12:06.922
Do you think differently?

00:12:07.393 --> 00:12:10.624
No, you're right.
I mean, that's normal, ya know?

00:12:10.963 --> 00:12:13.693
What? You really have been
acting strange lately.

00:12:13.899 --> 00:12:15.764
Ah, I had forgotten about that.

00:12:15.901 --> 00:12:18.734
Huh? I don't know what you're talking about.

00:12:35.654 --> 00:12:40.114
It's because there's no garden here
that I prefer our cottage.

00:12:40.292 --> 00:12:41.861
Yeah, you have a point.

00:12:41.861 --> 00:12:44.386
I wonder when we'll go again?

00:12:44.697 --> 00:12:48.434
That place has been turned
into a research facility.

00:12:48.434 --> 00:12:49.535
Really?

00:12:49.535 --> 00:12:52.971
Herve said it will be a while
before we can go again.

00:12:54.607 --> 00:12:55.941
That's too bad.

00:12:55.941 --> 00:12:59.578
But our uncle said that he'd look
for an even better place!

00:12:59.578 --> 00:13:00.312
Really?!

00:13:00.312 --> 00:13:00.813
Yeah!
Really?!

00:13:00.813 --> 00:13:01.313
Yeah!
That's great. I start to feel like I can't breathe.

00:13:01.313 --> 00:13:05.017
That's great. I start to feel like I can't breathe.

00:13:05.017 --> 00:13:06.416
I know what you mean.

00:13:06.652 --> 00:13:08.176
There is a swing, but...

00:13:08.687 --> 00:13:10.177
A swing like that...

00:13:10.422 --> 00:13:15.661
Our uncle must think that we're still little kids.

00:13:15.661 --> 00:13:18.264
Maybe in the eyes of adults, we are.

00:13:18.264 --> 00:13:21.631
I can't even figure out what I want anymore.

00:13:21.801 --> 00:13:24.270
Even though you had that long
list of things you wanted?

00:13:24.270 --> 00:13:26.205
I'm already sick of it all.

00:13:26.205 --> 00:13:29.868
Yeah, I'd sure like to go to
the amusement park.

00:13:30.543 --> 00:13:33.569
Ah, that would be fun!
We should go one of these days!

00:13:33.946 --> 00:13:36.471
We could ride the ferris wheel
together like we did last time.

00:13:36.916 --> 00:13:37.905
Mireille?!

00:13:38.517 --> 00:13:42.044
Mireille! What's wrong, Mireille?! Mireille!

00:13:42.488 --> 00:13:44.115
Somebody! Somebody help!

00:13:44.590 --> 00:13:46.285
Mireille! Mireille!

00:13:47.293 --> 00:13:49.328
Somebody! Somebody come
and help right away!

00:13:49.328 --> 00:13:51.091
Mireille is... Somebody!

00:13:51.697 --> 00:13:54.461
Mireille! Hang on! Mireille!

00:14:04.476 --> 00:14:05.443
Anna?

00:14:05.678 --> 00:14:07.908
She's all right. She's sleeping now.

00:14:08.547 --> 00:14:11.448
As for Mireille, she probably just
got herself over-excited.

00:14:11.817 --> 00:14:13.375
She'll probably sleep until morning.

00:14:14.787 --> 00:14:15.955
Dr. Bender?

00:14:15.955 --> 00:14:16.856
Yes?

00:14:16.856 --> 00:14:20.690
Of us, Mireille and Anna are
the last women, right?

00:14:21.327 --> 00:14:22.851
Yes, that's right.

00:14:23.062 --> 00:14:24.051
I know for women,

00:14:24.396 --> 00:14:28.594
the condition usually manifests
in their mid-teens.

00:14:30.369 --> 00:14:31.802
Is it going to happen soon?

00:14:32.705 --> 00:14:35.374
A new medication is being developed
even as we speak.

00:14:35.374 --> 00:14:37.069
I've heard enough about that already!

00:14:37.810 --> 00:14:41.473
I mean it's useless, isn't it?! The medications
have no effect on Mireille, right?!

00:14:54.560 --> 00:14:57.256
Excuse me, Uncle.

00:14:58.264 --> 00:14:59.665
Listen to me, Uncle.

00:14:59.665 --> 00:15:02.468
Sure. Why don't do have a seat?

00:15:02.468 --> 00:15:04.527
Let's make an attack on them, Uncle.

00:15:04.870 --> 00:15:06.462
If we do it now, we can win!

00:15:07.039 --> 00:15:08.374
We can't yet.

00:15:08.374 --> 00:15:09.432
Why?!

00:15:09.575 --> 00:15:11.873
Once Anna and Mireille's conditions have
manifested, it will be too late!

00:15:12.077 --> 00:15:15.706
If we fail, it will truly be the end of us.

00:15:16.649 --> 00:15:18.776
I'm trying to figure out the
best way to handle this.

00:15:19.184 --> 00:15:21.049
If Anna's condition is going to manifest

00:15:21.253 --> 00:15:23.448
and turn her into some sort of beast,

00:15:23.756 --> 00:15:26.418
I'II... I'll do anything!

00:15:29.561 --> 00:15:30.653
Uncle!

00:15:33.399 --> 00:15:35.200
Why don't you come and have a look

00:15:35.200 --> 00:15:37.293
at that girl, Lise, that you brought here?

00:15:47.713 --> 00:15:48.873
That's Lise.

00:15:51.250 --> 00:15:53.275
If this experiment is a success,

00:15:53.719 --> 00:15:56.813
we will have secured ourselves a new future.

00:15:57.556 --> 00:15:59.959
Our bloodline will go on.

00:15:59.959 --> 00:16:01.324
Is that to say...

00:16:01.660 --> 00:16:05.297
We're going to just give up
on Anna and Mireille?

00:16:05.297 --> 00:16:10.166
No, we're going to do our best
for Anna and Mireille.

00:16:10.369 --> 00:16:12.394
That plan has not changed at all.

00:16:12.604 --> 00:16:16.775
But they are running out of time.
What is the best that we can do?!

00:16:16.775 --> 00:16:19.573
Herve, I told you this earlier.

00:16:20.746 --> 00:16:22.373
For the time being, don't do anything.

00:16:22.915 --> 00:16:24.143
Uncle...

00:16:24.516 --> 00:16:27.610
That is an order. You had better
mind your selfish actions.

00:16:36.795 --> 00:16:40.788
It's not every day one sees
you at work this early.

00:16:41.100 --> 00:16:42.158
Well...

00:16:42.401 --> 00:16:43.527
What's going on?

00:16:44.103 --> 00:16:46.571
Lately, I haven't...

00:16:46.739 --> 00:16:51.438
Well, it is true that you haven't
been contributing to Grace.

00:16:51.844 --> 00:16:53.178
I'm sorry.

00:16:53.178 --> 00:16:57.046
And it looks like there are some
students not too happy with you.

00:16:58.083 --> 00:17:00.285
If whatever it is, is too much,

00:17:00.285 --> 00:17:02.617
I'll do whatever I can to help you out.

00:17:04.156 --> 00:17:06.784
There's a detective here again.

00:17:09.261 --> 00:17:11.627
Well, what we want to talk about
today is no big deal either.

00:17:12.231 --> 00:17:13.721
So, don't be nervous.

00:17:14.299 --> 00:17:18.133
But still, be honest in telling us what you know.

00:17:18.937 --> 00:17:19.995
I understand.

00:17:20.239 --> 00:17:22.434
The last time we met,

00:17:22.708 --> 00:17:26.269
you said that the last time you had
seen Lise was in class, right?

00:17:26.545 --> 00:17:28.740
The day before she disappeared.

00:17:29.114 --> 00:17:30.315
That's right.

00:17:30.315 --> 00:17:31.884
Is that true?

00:17:31.884 --> 00:17:32.718
Huh?

00:17:32.718 --> 00:17:36.654
No, it's just that in talking with a lot of kids,

00:17:37.222 --> 00:17:42.956
we heard that you and Lise went together,
after class, to South Side Park that day.

00:17:43.429 --> 00:17:45.329
What can you tell me about that?

00:17:45.898 --> 00:17:47.866
Why didn't you say anything?

00:17:49.368 --> 00:17:52.860
Hey, it's no big deal!
We're not accusing you of anything.

00:17:53.238 --> 00:17:58.335
When someone suffers a shock like that, one's
memory of that time often gets hazy.

00:18:00.012 --> 00:18:04.608
But still, I'd like you to try to
remember what you can.

00:18:05.384 --> 00:18:08.842
What were the two of you talking about?

00:18:11.090 --> 00:18:12.489
That day...

00:18:14.993 --> 00:18:15.994
What is this?!

00:18:15.994 --> 00:18:18.063
What is it? It's your paycheck.

00:18:18.063 --> 00:18:19.860
Yeah, why's it so low?!

00:18:20.032 --> 00:18:21.733
There's nothing low about it.

00:18:21.733 --> 00:18:26.466
Well, it's a lot lower than last month's!
This isn't funny!

00:18:27.206 --> 00:18:28.332
Hey!

00:18:29.174 --> 00:18:29.942
What?

00:18:29.942 --> 00:18:30.576
This is your timecard. Have a good look at it!
What?

00:18:30.576 --> 00:18:32.771
This is your timecard. Have a good look at it!

00:18:34.012 --> 00:18:35.147
What?

00:18:35.147 --> 00:18:37.783
Late, leaving early, not showing up at all...

00:18:37.783 --> 00:18:39.478
Now you know the cause and the result.

00:18:41.153 --> 00:18:43.555
But this, I won't even be able to cover rent!

00:18:43.555 --> 00:18:45.958
Well, if you want to pay it,
you're going to have to work.

00:18:45.958 --> 00:18:46.947
This conversation is over!

00:18:48.160 --> 00:18:49.661
With your work performance,

00:18:49.661 --> 00:18:51.492
I could fire you and you couldn't say a thing.

00:18:51.730 --> 00:18:52.831
Huh?!

00:18:52.831 --> 00:18:56.767
I'm being generous just giving you a job.

00:18:57.769 --> 00:18:59.271
Knock off the bullshit!

00:18:59.271 --> 00:18:59.905
What?

00:18:59.905 --> 00:19:00.472
This hole... I quit!
What?

00:19:00.472 --> 00:19:02.441
This hole... I quit!

00:19:02.441 --> 00:19:05.177
Yeah? And what about rent?
Are you gonna fall behind again?

00:19:05.177 --> 00:19:07.475
Mind your own business, you old bastard!

00:19:07.779 --> 00:19:09.047
What did you say?!

00:19:09.047 --> 00:19:11.880
There a lot of places where I can get a job!

00:19:12.384 --> 00:19:14.477
I'm not coming back even if you beg me to!

00:19:15.020 --> 00:19:16.510
Idiot!

00:19:20.492 --> 00:19:23.128
Well, all we can do is look for
that boyfriend of Lise's

00:19:23.128 --> 00:19:24.595
that she was talking about, don't you think?

00:19:24.830 --> 00:19:27.390
If there really is such a guy.

00:19:28.467 --> 00:19:29.729
Oh, sorry...

00:19:30.402 --> 00:19:33.735
Well, in any case, we don't have
a name or an address.

00:19:33.939 --> 00:19:36.441
There's got to be some kind of clue out there.

00:19:36.441 --> 00:19:39.578
Don't you think that girl, Kate,
is still hiding something?

00:19:39.578 --> 00:19:40.412
Huh?

00:19:40.412 --> 00:19:43.176
Whenever we meet her, there's always
something that just doesn't feel quite right.

00:19:44.049 --> 00:19:45.607
I wonder why?

00:19:51.390 --> 00:19:54.689
This kind of world...
There's nothing good about it.

00:20:29.428 --> 00:20:30.986
Rose, are you all right?!

00:20:32.364 --> 00:20:33.632
Get up! Now!

00:20:33.632 --> 00:20:34.792
Rachel!

00:21:17.643 --> 00:21:21.374
Those girls, they're terrible.

00:21:28.453 --> 00:21:30.555
Rock, rock the LM. C!

00:21:30.555 --> 00:21:32.853
One, two, everybody go!

00:21:40.966 --> 00:21:43.235
The time has come! It hasn't! But still!

00:21:43.235 --> 00:21:45.837
It always starts with the tears in your eyes

00:21:45.837 --> 00:21:47.939
If every weighed-out day

00:21:47.939 --> 00:21:50.142
You leave feeling sick, fly high

00:21:50.142 --> 00:21:51.710
Yesterday's failures? They don't mean a thing!

00:21:51.710 --> 00:21:53.845
Tomorrow's worries? They don't mean a thing!

00:21:53.845 --> 00:21:55.981
What's always important is this moment

00:21:55.981 --> 00:21:58.575
So it goes up to the top, top, top, top

00:22:07.092 --> 00:22:08.827
Rock, rock the LM. C!

00:22:08.827 --> 00:22:10.228
Gather around, my comrades

00:22:10.228 --> 00:22:11.363
If the dream you haven't had doesn't fade away

00:22:11.363 --> 00:22:13.131
Rock, rock the LM. C!

00:22:13.131 --> 00:22:15.000
So don't care, babe!

00:22:15.000 --> 00:22:18.637
I'm not going to ask you the reason

00:22:18.637 --> 00:22:22.874
We'll protect you

00:22:22.874 --> 00:22:25.510
So it's okay even if they don't like you

00:22:25.510 --> 00:22:30.015
Even if they laugh at you

00:22:30.015 --> 00:22:33.051
Just keep going down that road you believe in

00:22:33.051 --> 00:22:35.654
Your tears are

00:22:35.654 --> 00:22:39.925
Two of this world's treasures beyond compare

00:22:39.925 --> 00:22:42.694
I will simply keep on singing

00:22:42.694 --> 00:22:49.835
So I won't lose it and it will reach you

00:22:49.835 --> 00:22:52.070
Rock, rock the LM. C!

00:22:52.070 --> 00:22:54.172
Rock, rock the LM. C!

00:22:54.172 --> 00:22:56.402
Rock, rock the LM. C!

00:23:00.679 --> 00:23:03.648
A new night, the unchanging days...

00:23:04.583 --> 00:23:09.316
A little light illuminates the road just ahead.

00:23:10.088 --> 00:23:10.489
And the girls joined hands.

00:23:10.489 --> 00:23:12.290
Episode #8
Go Love
And the girls joined hands.

00:23:12.290 --> 00:23:14.520
Episode #8
Go Love
